  "prefLabel": "En 1002.24 Fault current",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1002.24 “Fault current” means electrical current that flows through a circuit and is produced by an electrical fault, such as phase to ground, double-phase to ground, 3-phase to ground, phase-to-phase, and 3-phase. A fault current is often several times larger in magnitude than the current that normally flows through a circuit.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
